{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/308396-more-nameless-gods","id":308396,"title":"More Nameless Gods?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-10T11:39:43-08:00","id":308396,"title":"More Nameless Gods?","content":"I must say that the Nameless Gods are one of the pieces of the setting which I really like, and while I understand why only 5 + Azar were given (one for each Decree), I still wonder which other &quot;lesser known&quot; gods could be added from the Egyptian Pantheon to the one of Irem (yes, in theory all of them, but I wonder which are interesting enough in your opinion and how would you add them).<br /> <br /> The first deity I would add is Nephthys. I mean, she is one of the four members of the Ennead and a major goddess- but she sometimes seems to be &quot;pushed away&quot; by her other three siblings. She is actually one of my favored Egyptian gods, so it may be why I'm annoyed when she doesn't shows up when her siblings does. I do wonder about which name she should get- the Nameless Flower, perhaps?<br /> <br /> While Horus is also an important god, he was sometimes combined with Ra so I can understand why he doesn't show up. As an independent god, his &quot;symbol animal&quot;, the Falcon, was already taken by Isis- but it seems that there isn't much connection between the egyptian animal connection and the iremite, so I can assume he could show up.<br /> <br /> Bastet is almost too easy to add as the &quot;Nameless Cat&quot;, with Sobek being close by as the Nameless Crocodile. I could see Thoth as the Nameless Monkey, Hathor requires a bit more thought, for Ptah is the Bull, and while she could be the Cow I still wonder is there could be some other animal.<br /> <br /> Neith and Khonsu are also gods which I like, but I can't really remember if there is some animal connected to them. If we leave animal connections behind (like I did with Nephthys), maybe the Nameless Huntress and the Nameless Traveler could work. Whiel I don't know much about Iusaaset, she does seem cool, if only because that for some reason I think that in Mummy she would be represented by some ancient, eldritch horror from beyond time who came before Duat- but maybe Ammut fills that niche. The same for Apep- that snake can stay is CWoD's Mummy. Ammut eats him for breakfast.<br /> <br /> Your thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T12:43:12-08:00","id":308455,"title":"","content":"Given that one of the books makes mention of cats being sacred even in the time of Irem, I'd love to see the feline cult and a Bast-analogue (or even better, a Sekhmet-analogue) get the Mummy treatment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https:/